      "textEn": "223\n\nSarppodashapadas sprushtah krupanam kaalachoditah. 9>. Meaning of the word:\nOnce--once; Nirgatam--after leaving; Gehatu--from the house; Duhantim--for milking; Nishi--at night; Gam--cow;\nKo; Pathi--on the road; Sarpa:--snake; Adashat--bitten; Pada--in the foot; Sprushtah--bitten in this way; Kripanam--\nPoor woman; Kal-choditah--being subdued by the ultimate time..\n\nOnce, when my poor mother was going to milk the cow at night, then from the supreme time,\nan inspired serpent bit my mother's foot. Meaning: This is the method of drawing a truthful soul to God. The poor child\nwas living only under the care of his affectionate mother, yet his mother was taken away from this world\nas a result of her supreme desire, so that the child could be completely dependent on the grace of God.\nThen, for the sake of his devotees, may they be free from all anxieties.\nHe who believes in grace, is established in the right direction. 10>. Meaning of the word\nTada--At that time; Tat--That; Aham--I; Ishasya- of God; Bhaktanam- of devotees; Sham--Compassion; Abeepsatah-- Wanted; Anugraham- special blessing; Manyamanah-- Thinking like this; Pratishtham- arrived; Disham Uttaraam- North\nThought that this was the special grace of God, because they are the ones who want the good of their devotees.\nAnd thinking like this, I started walking towards the north. Meaning: The faithful devotees of God accept the gracious order of God as they walk. That which is considered an inauspicious or difficult moment from a worldly perspective is accepted as a special grace of God. Worldly prosperity is a kind of physical fever, but by the grace of God,\nthe temperature of this fever gradually decreases, and at every step, spiritual health-\nbenefits continue to occur. Worldly people misunderstand this. There are explosive sounds, and there are villages and forest dwellers."
