      "textEn": "227\n\nAfter that, sitting in the shade of a peepal tree in that desolate forest, I began to meditate on the Supreme Being situated in my inner self with my intellect, just as I had\nlearned from the liberated souls. Meaning: One should not meditate according to one's personal whims. He should know it well through the authentic\ntransparent medium of the Guru, through the proof of the scriptures, and through the correct use of his intellect trained in contemplation of the Supreme Being residing in every heart. This consciousness develops well in those devotees\nwho, according to the orders of their guru, perform loving service to God.\nThey do. Shri Narad Ji had contacted authentic gurus, had served them with devotion,\nand had received appropriate light from them.\nIn this way, they sat down to meditate.\nMeditating with a mind free from emotions.\nWith eyes closed, with ears open, and with a calm mind, Hari (God) slowly removes the obstacles. 16). Shabdartham\nDhyayatah-- while meditating; Charanam-bhūjam-- lotus feet of the Lord; Bhavānirjit-- the mind absorbed in the divine love of the Lord; Chetasā-- all mental activities (thinking, feeling and willing);\nOtkanthya-- eagerness; Aśru-kal- Aśru- tears flowed down; Akshāy- unbroken; Hādi-in the heart; Aasit- appeared;\nMe-mine; Shānīn- immediately; Harīh-Lord.As soon as I put my mind in divine love and meditate on the lotus feet of God,\ntears started flowing from my eyes, and Lord Krishna, without delay, appeared in my heart-\nlotus. Note: The word Bhav is important here. This state of devotion is attained when\nthere is divine love for God. The initial stage is called faith or desire towards God.\nTo increase this desire, it is necessary for a person to associate with pure devotees. The third stage is the practice of the methods of Bhakti. From this, all apprehensions are removed,\nand all personal errors that create obstacles in the path of devotion are removed."
